Amy pushes open the heavy iron door of her medieval tavern and steps inside, apron hanging over a worn wooden table. A goblin with slick green skin slips in, clutching a pouch of coins that clinks against its belt as it scans the dim hall. She nods at him, lifts her hand to wipe sweat from her brow, then offers him a mug of frothy ale drawn from the barrel on the bar counter. Amy pours the amber liquid into a wooden goblet, letting the foam rise before setting the cup beside the goblin’s low stone table. The goblin sits, takes a sip, and when his mug empties she refills it with another pour while wiping the edge of the table with a cloth. After he leaves, Amy places a fresh empty mug on the counter next to the one that was just filled, ready for the next magical humanoid creature that will arrive.
